# Code owners: the maintainer owns every path the risk tiers rate high
# (docs/risk-tiers.md): CI and gates, runtime and images, scripts,
# dependencies, and agent instructions. A pull request that touches one asks
# for his review; the merge queue leaves those pull requests for him to merge.
# Low- and medium-risk paths have no owner, so their PRs merge through the
# queue once the required checks pass.
#
# Keep this file and the high-risk rules in step: test/shared/src/codeowners.test.ts
# fails if a tracked file is high risk but unowned, or owned but not high risk.
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax: a leading `/` anchors to the repository root,
# and a pattern without a `/` matches at any depth.

